{
  "slug": "beef-and-rice-bowl",
  "name": "Beef and rice bowl",
  "description": "Browned lean ground beef with broccoli, carrot and onion over warm brown rice, seasoned with garlic and chili powder.",
  "iconKey": "dome",
  "instructions": [
    "Warm the olive oil in a wide skillet over medium-high heat.",
    "Add the onion and carrot, and cook for 4 to 5 minutes until they soften.",
    "Add the ground beef and the chili powder, then brown the beef for 6 to 7 minutes, breaking it apart as it cooks.",
    "Stir in the broccoli and garlic, and cook for another 4 to 5 minutes, until the broccoli softens but keeps its bite.",
    "Divide the warm brown rice between two bowls, then spoon the beef mixture over the top."
